Rem ==================================================================
Rem seedmiptest.shoddy — test program for seedmip.shoddy
Rem
Rem Assert-driven, in the seedsimplextest / seedsparsetest pattern: it
Rem prints what it is doing and stops the run at the first assertion
Rem that fails, ending with ALL ASSERTIONS PASSED when it does not.
Rem
Rem THE BALES PROBLEM IS THE CASE WORTH HAVING, and it is the one the
Rem mill ships as files/bales.mps. Its relaxation buys a fraction of a
Rem bale; rounding that up costs 12; the greedy whole-bale filler costs
Rem 10; the answer is 9. A search that is not really running gets one
Rem of the other three, so the number 9 is doing real work here.
Rem
Rem THE ROUND TRIP IS THE OTHER HALF. MIPFIXED hands back an ordinary
Rem problem, and the assertion that matters is that LPSOLVE reads it —
Rem that is the whole reason this seed speaks seedsimplex's dict shapes
Rem instead of inventing its own.
Rem
Rem THE GUARD LIST IS THE TEST LIST. mip.shoddy Errors on an integer
Rem index naming no variable and on MipFixed handed a non-optimum, and
Rem the LP under it Errors on a problem whose parts do not line up.
Rem Each is walked once below through Refuses, which also asserts the
Rem session survived being told no.
Rem
Rem NOT TESTED, AND NAMED HERE INSTEAD: MAXITER and MAXNODES, which
Rem need a hundred thousand of something apiece. A problem big enough
Rem to reach either is far larger than a test should be, and capping
Rem the keyboard lower than the machine would mean testing something
Rem other than what ships.
Rem
Rem Run: bin\mill run tst\seedmiptest.shoddy   (from the repo root)
Rem ==================================================================

Include "../machines/cuttle.shoddy"
Include "../machines/reckoner.shoddy"
Include "../machines/seq.shoddy"
Include "../machines/str.shoddy"
Include "../machines/seeds/seedmip.shoddy"
Include "../machines/seeds/seedsimplex.shoddy"
Include "../machines/seeds/seedmatrix.shoddy"
Include "../machines/seeds/seeddict.shoddy"

Def Ran(st As RckState, line As String) As RckState
    Select Case RckEval(st, line)
        Case RckNext(st2, out)
            st2
        Case RckStop(st2, why, out)
            st2
        Case Else
            st

Def Bad(st As RckState, line As String) As Boolean
    Select Case RckEval(st, line)
        Case RckStop(st2, why, out)
            True
        Case Else
            False

Def Why(st As RckState, line As String) As String
    Select Case RckEval(st, line)
        Case RckStop(st2, why, out)
            why
        Case Else
            ""

Def Text(st As RckState) As String
    Join(Map(CutCells(RckStack(st)), Fn(c) => CutShow(c, RckFmt(st))), " | ")

Def Q(s As String) As String
    Chr(34) & s & Chr(34)

Def Refuses(st As RckState, line As String, why As String) As Boolean
    Bad(st, line) And Instr(Why(st, line), why) > 0 And Text(Ran(st, line)) = Text(st) And Text(Ran(Ran(st, line), "1 1 +")) = Text(Ran(st, "1 1 +"))

Def Nl() As String
    Chr(10)

Def Lines(xs As List Of String) As String
    Join(xs, Nl())

Rem Bales of fibre, as the mill's files/bales.mps states it: minimize
Rem 5A + 4B + 2C subject to 6A + 4B + 3C >= 10, with A and B whole and
Rem C binary. Written out here as an MPS text so MPSMIP is exercised on
Rem the marker AND the BV bound in one file.

Def BalesText() As String
    Lines({ "NAME BALES", "ROWS", " N COST", " G FIBRE", "COLUMNS",
            "    MARKER                 'MARKER'                 'INTORG'",
            " A COST 5 FIBRE 6", " B COST 4 FIBRE 4",
            "    MARKER                 'MARKER'                 'INTEND'",
            " C COST 2 FIBRE 3", "RHS", " RHS FIBRE 10",
            "BOUNDS", " BV BND C", "ENDATA" })

Rem The same problem built by hand, for the words that take one that
Rem way: two variables, 6A + 4B >= 10, both whole.

Def ByHand() As String
    "{ 5 4 } 1 2 { 6 4 } MAT { 10 } LPPROBLEM { 1 2 } MIPPROBLEM"

Def Main()
    Let s0 = RckSeedDict(RckSeedMatrix(RckSeedMip(RckSeedSimplex(RckNew()))))
    Let g = Ran(s0, "1 2")

    Print("--- the five words are registered and carry their metadata ---")
    Assert(RckKnows(s0, "MIPPROBLEM") And RckKnows(s0, "MIPSOLVE") And RckKnows(s0, "MIPFIXED"), "THE THREE THAT STATE, SOLVE AND PIN")
    Assert(RckKnows(s0, "MPSMIP") And RckKnows(s0, "MPSMIPLOAD"), "AND THE TWO THAT READ AN INTEGER FILE")
    Assert(All(RckDict(s0), Fn(e) => WordEffect(e) <> "" And WordDesc(e) <> ""), "NO WORD IS WITHOUT AN EFFECT LINE AND A DESCRIPTION")
    Assert(All(RckDict(s0), Fn(e) => Length(RckHelp(s0, WordName(e))) = 3), "AND HELP ANSWERS FOR EVERY ONE OF THEM")
    Assert(All(RckDict(s0), Fn(e) => Instr(Lower(WordEffect(e)), "handle") = 0), "NO WORD'S EFFECT STRING MENTIONS A HANDLE")

    Print("--- a problem built by hand, relaxed and then made whole ---")
    Assert(Text(Ran(s0, ByHand() & " " & Q("ints") & " DGET")) = "{ 1 2 }", "THE INTEGER VARIABLES ARE REMEMBERED")
    Rem The relaxation first, so the integer answer has something to
    Rem differ from: all A, one and two thirds of it, costing 8.3333.
    Assert(Text(Ran(s0, ByHand() & " " & Q("prob") & " DGET LPSOLVE " & Q("cost") & " DGET 10000 * ROUND")) = "83333",
           "THE RELAXATION BUYS A FRACTION OF A BALE FOR 8.3333")
    Assert(Text(Ran(s0, ByHand() & " MIPSOLVE " & Q("status") & " DGET")) = Q("OPTIMAL"), "AND WHOLE BALES CAN BE BOUGHT")
    Assert(Text(Ran(s0, ByHand() & " MIPSOLVE " & Q("cost") & " DGET")) = "9", "FOR 9, WHICH IS NEITHER THE RELAXATION NOR THE RELAXATION ROUNDED")
    Assert(Text(Ran(s0, ByHand() & " MIPSOLVE " & Q("x") & " DGET")) = "{ 1 1 }", "ONE OF EACH BALE")
    Assert(Not Bad(s0, ByHand() & " MIPSOLVE " & Q("nodes") & " DGET"), "THE SEARCH REPORTS WHAT IT COST")
    Assert(Text(Ran(s0, ByHand() & " MIPSOLVE " & Q("nodes") & " DGET 1 >")) = "True", "AND IT TOOK MORE THAN THE ROOT NODE")

    Print("--- an empty integer list is just the linear program again ---")
    Assert(Text(Ran(s0, "{ 5 4 } 1 2 { 6 4 } MAT { 10 } LPPROBLEM { } MIPPROBLEM MIPSOLVE " & Q("nodes") & " DGET")) = "1",
           "NOTHING TO BRANCH ON, SO ONE NODE")

    Print("--- MIPFIXED, and the round trip that is its whole point ---")
    Rem MIPSOLVE answers no shadow prices, deliberately. MIPFIXED pins
    Rem the integers and hands back a problem LPSOLVE reads like any
    Rem other, and THAT has prices worth reading.
    Assert(Text(Ran(s0, ByHand() & " MIPSOLVE " & Q("dualprices") & " DHAS")) = "False", "A MIP SOLUTION CARRIES NO SHADOW PRICES AT ALL, NOT EVEN AN EMPTY ONE")
    Assert(Text(Ran(s0, ByHand() & " MIPSOLVE " & Q("reduced") & " DHAS")) = "False", "AND NO REDUCED COSTS EITHER")
    Assert(Text(Ran(s0, ByHand() & " MIPSOLVE " & Q("nodes") & " DHAS")) = "True", "WHAT IT CARRIES INSTEAD IS WHAT THE SEARCH COST")
    Let fx = ByHand() & " DUP MIPSOLVE MIPFIXED"
    Assert(Text(Ran(s0, fx & " LPSOLVE " & Q("status") & " DGET")) = Q("OPTIMAL"), "THE PINNED PROBLEM IS A PROBLEM LPSOLVE READS")
    Assert(Text(Ran(s0, fx & " LPSOLVE " & Q("cost") & " DGET")) = "9", "TO THE COST THE SEARCH REPORTED")
    Assert(Text(Ran(s0, fx & " " & Q("rhs") & " DGET")) = "{ 10 1 -1 1 -1 }", "PINNING TWO VARIABLES ADDED TWO ROWS APIECE TO THE ONE THERE WAS")
    Assert(Not Bad(s0, fx & " LPSOLVE " & Q("dualprices") & " DGET"), "AND ITS SHADOW PRICES ARE THERE TO READ")

    Print("--- an integer MPS file, marker and BV bound in one ---")
    Assert(Not Bad(s0, Q(BalesText()) & " MPSMIP"), "MPSMIP READS A FILE THE PLAIN WORDS REFUSE")
    Assert(Text(Ran(s0, Q(BalesText()) & " MPSMIP " & Q("ints") & " DGET")) = "{ 1 2 3 }", "TWO COLUMNS FROM THE MARKER AND ONE FROM THE BV BOUND")
    Assert(Text(Ran(s0, Q(BalesText()) & " MPSMIP MIPSOLVE " & Q("cost") & " DGET")) = "9", "AND IT SOLVES TO THE ANSWER ITS OWN HEADER WORKS OUT BY HAND")
    Assert(Text(Ran(s0, Q(BalesText()) & " MPSMIP MIPSOLVE " & Q("x") & " DGET")) = "{ 1 1 0 }", "LEAVING THE CHEAP-LOOKING JOB LOT ON THE SHELF")
    Assert(Text(Ran(s0, Q("mills/simplex-from-mps/files/bales.mps") & " MPSMIPLOAD MIPSOLVE " & Q("cost") & " DGET")) = "9",
           "AND THE COMMITTED FIXTURE SOLVES THE SAME WAY OFF DISK")
    Rem A file with no integer columns is a mipproblem with nothing to
    Rem branch on, which is what lets one word read any file.
    Assert(Text(Ran(s0, Q(Lines({ "ROWS", " N C", " G R", "COLUMNS", " X C 1 R 1", "RHS", " RHS R 1", "ENDATA" })) & " MPSMIP " & Q("ints") & " DGET")) = "{ }",
           "AND A FILE THAT MARKS NOTHING READS AS A PROBLEM WITH NO INTEGERS")

    Print("--- every abort mip.shoddy has, refused instead ---")
    Assert(Refuses(g, "{ 5 4 } 1 2 { 6 4 } MAT { 10 } LPPROBLEM { 3 } MIPPROBLEM", "DOES NOT EXIST — THERE ARE 2"), "AN INTEGER VARIABLE THAT IS NOT THERE, SAYING HOW MANY ARE")
    Assert(Refuses(g, "{ 5 4 } 1 2 { 6 4 } MAT { 10 } LPPROBLEM { 0 } MIPPROBLEM", "DOES NOT EXIST"), "AND VARIABLE ZERO, WHICH 1-BASED COUNTING HAS NONE OF")
    Assert(Refuses(g, "{ 5 4 } 1 2 { 6 4 } MAT { 10 } LPPROBLEM { 1.5 } MIPPROBLEM", "DOES NOT EXIST"), "AND A FRACTIONAL ONE, WHICH NAMES NO VARIABLE")
    Rem MipFixed Errors on anything that is not an optimum. An
    Rem infeasible problem is the way to get one honestly: 2X >= 1 and
    Rem 2X <= 1 pin X at a half, which no integer reaches.
    Let half = "{ 1 } 2 1 { 2 -2 } MAT { 1 -1 } LPPROBLEM { 1 } MIPPROBLEM"
    Assert(Text(Ran(s0, half & " MIPSOLVE " & Q("status") & " DGET")) = Q("INFEASIBLE"), "A PROBLEM WITH NO WHOLE ANSWER SAYS SO PLAINLY")
    Assert(Refuses(g, half & " DUP MIPSOLVE MIPFIXED", "THIS SOLUTION IS INFEASIBLE"), "AND PINNING ONE'S INTEGERS IS REFUSED, NAMING THE STATUS")

    Print("--- and every shape that is not what the word wants ---")
    Assert(Refuses(g, "3 { 1 } MIPPROBLEM", "NOT A PROBLEM"), "A NUMBER WHERE A PROBLEM SHOULD BE")
    Assert(Refuses(g, "{ 5 4 } 1 2 { 6 4 } MAT { 10 } LPPROBLEM 3 MIPPROBLEM", "needs a LIST"), "AND A NUMBER WHERE THE INTEGER LIST SHOULD BE")
    Assert(Refuses(g, "3 MIPSOLVE", "NOT AN INTEGER PROBLEM"), "A NUMBER WHERE A MIPPROBLEM SHOULD BE")
    Assert(Refuses(g, ByHand() & " 3 MIPFIXED", "NOT A SOLUTION"), "AND A NUMBER WHERE A SOLUTION SHOULD BE")
    Assert(Refuses(g, "3 MPSMIP", "needs a STRING, got NUMBER"), "AND A CELL THAT IS NOT TEXT AT ALL")
    Assert(Refuses(g, Q("tst/csv/does-not-exist.mps") & " MPSMIPLOAD", "CANNOT READ"), "A PATH THAT IS NOT THERE")
    Assert(Refuses(g, Q(Lines({ "RANGES" })) & " MPSMIP", "RANGES SECTION NOT SUPPORTED"), "AND THE VALIDATOR STILL GUARDS THE INTEGER WORDS TOO")

    Print("--- nothing above cost the session anything ---")
    Assert(Text(Ran(g, "1 1 +")) = "2 | 2 | 1", "THE STACK IS STILL THERE AND STILL EVALUATING")

    Print("")
    Print("ALL ASSERTIONS PASSED")
